  "hints": [
    "Treat the array as a linked list: index `i` points to `nums[i]`.",
    "The repeated value is where two pointers enter a cycle. Use Floyd's tortoise and hare.",
    "slow = fast = nums[0]\ndo: slow = nums[slow]; fast = nums[nums[fast]] until slow == fast\nslow = nums[0]\nwhile slow != fast: slow = nums[slow]; fast = nums[fast]\nreturn slow",
    "Two indices point to the duplicate value, which creates a cycle whose entry is the answer. O(n) time, O(1) space. Binary searching on the value range with counting also works in O(n log n)."
  ],
